    "summary": "ROOM-7 covers createBookings(): it validates bookings (room, owner, half-hour UTC start, a length of 30–240 min in 30-min steps), refuses overlaps within the same room, lists a room's bookings by start time, and lets only the owner cancel. Vitest unit tests against the real module with memoryStore() must prove each rule and its refusal, checking the BookingError message that says why.",
    "inScope": [
      "book() validation and refusals",
      "overlap rules",
      "list() ordering",
      "cancel() permission and freeing time"
    ],
    "outOfScope": [
      "The app's database BookingStore (not in repo)"
    ],
    "assumptions": [
      "Tests use the real createBookings with the default memoryStore(); nothing is faked.",
      "Refusal reasons are checked against the exact message src/bookings.ts gives, because only the message tells one BookingError from another.",
      "The at() UTC time builder moves to test/support/time.ts, and the existing test/bookings.test.ts imports it from there."
    ],
    "openQuestions": [],
    "risks": [
      {
        "description": "Off-by-one at boundaries (30/240 min, back-to-back bookings)",
        "impact": "high",
        "mitigation": "Boundary cases on both sides"
      },
      {
        "description": "Someone who didn't make a booking cancels it",
        "impact": "high",
        "mitigation": "TC13 checks the refusal and that the booking stays"
      }
    ],
    "acceptanceCriteria": [
